# Cloudflare Workers static-assets routing.
#
# Intentionally empty of active rules. Cloudflare Workers `[assets]`
# (wrangler.toml) already handles both concerns this file used to cover:
#
#   * `not_found_handling = "single-page-application"` sends any unmatched
#     path to /index.html so React Router takes over (replaces the old
#     `/* /index.html 200` SPA fallback that Cloudflare's validator now
#     rejects as a self-loop).
#   * `html_handling = "drop-trailing-slash"` canonicalises URLs by
#     stripping the trailing slash — /en/shop-and-ship/ 307s to
#     /en/shop-and-ship, then the assets binding serves
#     en/shop-and-ship/index.html from the prerender.
#
# The former rule `/*/  /:splat  301` we had here tried to do the
# trailing-slash normalisation itself, and formed a redirect loop with
# html_handling's default `auto-trailing-slash` — every trailing-slash
# URL (view-source:https://.../en/shop-and-ship/) hit "Too Many
# Redirects". Removed 2026-09-07.
#
# Only add a rule here for genuinely one-off redirects (renamed URL,
# retired page). Every rule Cloudflare's validator considers a self-loop
# will block the deploy.
